-- anotoki_translations 005 - the words of the legal pages, under the anotoki library's namespaces anotoki.legal. and
-- anotoki.legalLinks.
--
-- What the legal pages say (@anotoki/lib/legal/pages: the Terms, Privacy and Contact pages every anotoki site
-- shows, with its own facts) - their headings, the family's shared wording, the browser storage and the companies
-- the sites name - and the footer's three links to them (@anotoki/lib/legal). Their Slovak addresses nobody (no ty,
-- no Vy): the pages fit the informal sites and the formal survey alike. anotoki-lib's
-- php/resources/library-words.json holds them - the Angular half's built-in words are made from the same file, and
-- a test of the library holds this file to it.
--
-- As in 002: a key's description is the library's, and is written again whenever a library migration carries it;
-- a key's strings are the site's once it has any - written here only for a library key that has no string at all.
-- So a site that took a key over before this file ran keeps its words.
--
-- Released with anotoki-lib 0.6.0, and never edited once released: a change is a new file.

